Gizmo Fizzcrank, three-foot-tall and lime-green-haired, whistled as he skipped down the jungle path. Behind him, Sasha the succubus sauntered, tail flicking.  
A troll rogue leapt from the ferns, blades flashing. Sasha’s lashes glowed—Seduction. The rogue froze, drooling.  
Gizmo calmly dropped three DoTs, watched the timer, then popped a /point laugh.  
As the corpse hit the dirt, a second rogue unstealthed behind them.  
“No worries,” Gizmo grinned. Sasha winked—another 15-second Seduction.  
Chain-charmed, the second assassin knelt helplessly while the dots ticked.  
“See, no need for a blueberry,” Gizmo boasted.  
Just then, a raptor pack charged. Sasha couldn’t charm beasts; the gnome squeaked, sprinting toward the river with four scaly pursuers.  
He wished, for once, that his big purple punching bag had been there to tank.

Answer: Because Seduction works on humanoids, succubi are actually everywhere—just invisible on the minimap while they’re busy charming every ganker. [end of text]


